      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://ydjemmada.github.io/DZJC/PRIVACY_POLICY_PUBLIC.html</guid>
      <description>&lt;div data-dzjc-lang-panel=&#34;en&#34; hidden&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Last updated: 2026-07-26&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Product: &lt;strong&gt;DZ Journal Check&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Publisher: &lt;strong&gt;Yahia Djemmada&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Contact: &lt;a href=&#34;mailto:yahia.djem@gmail.com&#34;&gt;yahia.djem@gmail.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;summary&#34;&gt;Summary&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;DZ Journal Check is an independent Chrome extension that checks journal names, ISSNs, E-ISSNs, and DOI metadata against a bundled local DGRSDT/MESRS journal classification database.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The extension is designed for local journal classification on Google Scholar. It does not collect browsing history, Google Scholar searches, author names, article titles, account data, authentication information, financial information, health information, personal communications, or personally identifiable information.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Publications</title>
      <link>https://ydjemmada.github.io/publications/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://ydjemmada.github.io/publications/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;You can find my full list of publications on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=3kStp0sAAAAJ&amp;amp;hl=en&#34;&gt;Google Scholar&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;publications-container&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;article class=&#34;publication-card&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;pub-year&#34;&gt;2025&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;pub-content&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;h3 class=&#34;pub-title&#34;&gt;Partial Deranged Bell Numbers and Their Combinatorial Properties&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;            &lt;div class=&#34;pub-meta&#34;&gt;Djemmada, Yahia; Kargın, Levent; Can, Mümün&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;            &lt;div class=&#34;pub-journal&#34;&gt;arXiv preprint arXiv:2507.21643&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;            &#xA;            &lt;p class=&#34;pub-abstract&#34;&gt;We introduce partial deranged Bell numbers and investigate their combinatorial properties, providing generating functions and recurrence relations.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;            &#xA;&#xA;            &lt;div class=&#34;pub-actions&#34;&gt;&#xA;                &#xA;                &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.21643&#34; class=&#34;pub-btn&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;PDF&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;                &#xA;                &#xA;                &lt;button class=&#34;pub-btn cite-toggle&#34; onclick=&#34;toggleCite(this)&#34;&gt;Cite&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;            &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;            &lt;div class=&#34;bibtex-block&#34; style=&#34;display: none;&#34;&gt;&#xA;                &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;@article{djemmada2025partial,&#xA;  title={Partial Deranged Bell Numbers and Their Combinatorial Properties},&#xA;  author={Djemmada, Yahia and Karg{\i}n, Levent and Can, M{\&amp;amp;#34;u}m{\&amp;amp;#34;u}n},&#xA;  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:2507.21643},&#xA;  year={2025}&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;            &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/article&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;article class=&#34;publication-card&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;pub-year&#34;&gt;2024&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;pub-content&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;h3 class=&#34;pub-title&#34;&gt;An identity for two sequences and its combinatorial interpretation&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;            &lt;div class=&#34;pub-meta&#34;&gt;Djemmada, Yahia; Mehdaoui, Abdelghani; Németh, László; Szalay, László&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;            &lt;div class=&#34;pub-journal&#34;&gt;Annales Mathematicae et Informaticae&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;            &#xA;            &lt;p class=&#34;pub-abstract&#34;&gt;We establish a new identity relating two combinatorial sequences and provide a bijective proof demonstrating its combinatorial interpretation.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
